        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ryobi and DeWalt are not competing for the same buyer, and the spec sheets prove it less than the price tags do. Ryobi's HP brushless drill and impact driver match or beat DeWalt's ratings on paper at roughly half the kit price, and for a homeowner that makes Ryobi ONE+ HP the smarter platform, especially once you add household and outdoor tools on the same battery.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            DeWalt earns its premium in places a spec sheet does not show: tougher construction, a repair path, a free service year, availability at every hardware store and a professional range that runs all the way to FLEXVOLT saws. If tools are part of how you earn a living, or you are building a workshop you expect to keep for decades, that is money well spent.
          </p>
